# Workflow gates

**Purpose:** Define when agents or humans may claim work is **merge-ready**. This rule is the agent-facing contract; policy is also in [GOVERNANCE.md §10.5](../../adrs/GOVERNANCE.md#105-merge-ready-gates-orchestrated-efforts) and checklist IDs **MG-01**–**MG-05** in [`docs/validation-checklist.md`](../docs/validation-checklist.md). ADR lifecycle and gap recording: [adr-compliance.mdc](./adr-compliance.mdc).

## Two gate vocabularies (do not conflate)

| Vocabulary | Range | Tracks |
| -------- | ----- | ------ |
| **Lifecycle gates** | **0–6** | Pipeline stage completion in an orchestration run (`task-manifest.json` → `gate_status`) |
| **Merge-ready checks** (this rule) | **MG-01**–**MG-05** | Whether work may be claimed **merge-ready** (checklist IDs are canonical) |

**Lifecycle Gate 5** (Validator / validation green) ≠ **MG-05** (tooling). **Lifecycle Gate 6** (human approval) runs after merge-ready checks **MG-01**–**MG-05** are green; it is not a substitute for them.

> **Naming:** Use **MG-01**–**MG-05** in PRs and agent text. Legacy “merge-ready Gate 1–5” numbering (which did not match MG order) is retired.

Full mapping (lifecycle ↔ merge-ready ↔ MG-* ↔ skips): [`docs/validation-checklist.md` — Lifecycle gates, merge-ready gates, and `gate_status`](../docs/validation-checklist.md#lifecycle-gates-merge-ready-gates-and-gate_status). Narrative: [`docs/ORCHESTRATED_DEVELOPMENT.md`](../docs/ORCHESTRATED_DEVELOPMENT.md).

## When this rule applies

| Work | Gates |
| ---- | ----- |
| **Orchestrated** run under `.cursor/orchestrations/{task-id}/` | Full set below (**MG-01**–**MG-05**) |
| **Non-orchestrated** change touching architecture, auth, sync, AI, offline/SW, Dexie ownership, or secrets | **MG-01**, **MG-02**, **MG-05**; test/validation evidence in PR text (**MG-04** style) |
| **Trivial** (typo, comment-only, isolated non-architectural fix) | [adr-compliance.mdc](./adr-compliance.mdc) only; note **Orchestration not required** in PR or ADR when relevant |

“Durable architecture” matches [adr-compliance.mdc](./adr-compliance.mdc) high-impact areas: architecture, data flow, authentication, sync, AI, offline behavior (including service worker policy when behavior changes).

## MG-02 — ADR before durable architecture

- **Before** merge or any **merge-ready** claim, an ADR must be **created or updated** in the same effort when the change alters durable architecture (or a successor ADR explicitly governs the area).
- If the ADR cannot ship in scope: file a **Proposed** ADR or document an explicit follow-up with timeline in `plan.md`, the PR body, or the ADR **Merge / workflow gates** section — not code comments alone.
- **Proposed** ADRs are not binding; they do not authorize violating **Accepted** ADRs.

**Planner:** List cited Accepted ADRs in `plan.md` → **ADR references** before Builder starts. **Builder:** Do not implement durable architecture outside those ADRs without Orchestrator/human replan.

## MG-01 — Alignment gaps

- Implementation must match **Accepted** ADRs cited in `plan.md`, or deviation must be recorded in [`docs/readme-adr-alignment-gaps.md`](../docs/readme-adr-alignment-gaps.md) (owner, severity, affected areas, remediation, blocking flag).
- Do **not** hide drift in implementation comments only. See [adr-compliance.mdc](./adr-compliance.mdc) and [GOVERNANCE.md §5.6](../../adrs/GOVERNANCE.md).

## MG-03 — Validation evidence, orchestrated

For orchestrated runs, do **not** claim merge-ready until:

1. [`.cursor/orchestrations/{task-id}/validation-report.md`](../orchestrations/_template/validation-report.md) exists with sections: **Verdict**, **AC audit**, **ADR compliance**, **Checklist audit**, **Regressions**, **Required remediations**, **Recommended remediations**.
2. **Verdict** is **PASS** or **PASS_WITH_NOTES** (not **FAIL**). **PASS_WITH_NOTES** requires no ❌ ACs; residual ⚠️ items must be listed with justification. Merge-ready may proceed to `awaiting_human` only when **MG-01**–**MG-05** are satisfied; Gate 6 human records acceptance of residual risk (`conditions` / notes).
3. **Checklist audit** covers every applicable **MG-*** and domain row from [`docs/validation-checklist.md`](../docs/validation-checklist.md); any applicable ❌ on **MG-*** or on items required by `plan.md` / Accepted ADRs blocks **PASS** and **PASS_WITH_NOTES** unless replanned.

**Builder, Tester, and Planner** must **not** state merge-ready, “done”, “ready to merge”, or “ready to ship” for the task.

## MG-04 — Test evidence, orchestrated

For orchestrated runs, do **not** claim merge-ready until:

1. `test-report.md` exists with AC coverage map, commands run, and residual risk for intentional gaps.
2. When `test-matrix.md` has **Planned coverage** (non-trivial tasks), **Actual coverage** is filled or gaps are listed in `test-report.md` / **Gaps vs plan** (see **TST-05** in the validation checklist and [test-matrix.mdc](./test-matrix.mdc)).

Validator cross-checks test evidence per [`.cursor/agents/validator.md`](../agents/validator.md); Orchestrator must not route to `awaiting_human` without `test-report.md` (Validator activation requires it).

## MG-05 — Tooling

- `pnpm run check` and `pnpm run lint` pass for touched paths, or pre-existing failures outside scope are documented in `build-log.md`, `test-report.md`, or the PR.

## Small orchestrated runs

When `risk_tier.level` is `small` and stages are skipped per [`.cursor/agents/orchestrator.md`](../agents/orchestrator.md) rules 19–20:

- **Validator skipped (Path A):** Do **not** claim full orchestrated merge-ready. Satisfy **MG-01**, **MG-02**, **MG-04**, **MG-05** via PR + human review; **MG-03** via documented human substitute audit (not `validation-report.md`). Orchestrator may still set `awaiting_human` after Tester.
- **Validator runs (Path B):** **MG-03**–**MG-05** apply when `validation-report.md` is **PASS** / **PASS_WITH_NOTES**.
- **Tester skipped:** **MG-04** via PR test evidence (commands, spec paths, or explicit untested risk).

See [`docs/validation-checklist.md` — Small-run skips](../docs/validation-checklist.md#small-run-skips-risk_tierlevel-small).

## Orchestrator and human completion

Merge-ready for an **orchestrated run** is a **two-step** gate after Builder/Tester:

1. **Validator path:** **MG-03**–**MG-05** satisfied → Orchestrator may set `status` to `awaiting_human` (not `complete`).
2. **Human path:** `human_approval.status` is `approved` in `task-manifest.json` and Gate 6 is recorded in `human-approval.md` (mirrors manifest fields) → Orchestrator may set `status` to `complete`.

If `validation-report.md` verdict is **FAIL**, Orchestrator routes remediation per [orchestrator.md](../agents/orchestrator.md); do not claim merge-ready until a subsequent Validator **PASS** / **PASS_WITH_NOTES**.

## Non-orchestrated PRs and chat claims

When work is **not** under `.cursor/orchestrations/`, a merge-ready claim (in PR description or agent summary) must still:

- Satisfy **MG-01**, **MG-02**, and **MG-05**.
- Link test commands run, spec paths, or explicit **untested risk** per AC or behavior touched (**MG-04** style without requiring `test-report.md` unless the team adopted an orchestration folder for that change).

## Orchestration artifacts in git

**Default:** `.cursor/orchestrations/{task-id}/` stays local during the run; merge-ready claims in PRs use pasted summaries from `test-report.md` / `validation-report.md`. After **Gate 6** approval, the Orchestrator **asks** whether to commit (application code; optionally the task folder). Agents run `git commit` only when the human explicitly confirms — see [`.cursor/orchestrations/_template/README.md`](../orchestrations/_template/README.md) and [orchestrator.md](../agents/orchestrator.md) rule 14.

